# Font de la Vila Catchment Forest Inventory & Wildfire  Dataset
### Location: Andratx, Mallorca (Balearic Islands, Spain)

## Overview
This repository contains a comprehensive suite of spatial, environmental, and ecological inventory data collected within the **Font de la Vila Catchment**. The dataset is structurally designed to support environmental analysis, wildfire risk modeling, biomass estimation, and long-term post-fire vegetation recovery monitoring in Mediterranean ecosystems.

The study area captures a complex landscape marked by historical wildfire events—specifically tracking major burn footprints from **1994** and **2013**—across varying terrain configurations, including traditional agricultural dry-stone terracing.

---

## Quick Project Metadata
* **Temporal Scope:** Field inventories were systematically conducted between **April and July 2024**.
* **Coordinate Reference System:** UTM Zone 31N (Datum: ETRS89 / WGS84).
* **Core Species Monitored:** *Pinus halepensis* (Piha), *Quercus ilex* (Quil), *Olea europaea* (Oleu), and *Ampelodesmos mauritanicus* (Amma).

---

## Repository Architecture & Data Documentation

To keep the data highly navigable, each data file is paired with its own standalone Markdown documentation (`.md`) file containing exact column data dictionaries, variable types, and methodological definitions.

### 📋 Dataset Directory

| Data File (CSV) | Data Dictionary & Metadata | Description Summary |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 📄 [`MANFV_PlotInfo.csv`](./MANFV_PlotInfo.csv) | 📖 [PlotInfo Metadata](./MANFV_PlotInfo.md) | Topographical metrics (elevation, slope, aspect), fuel classes, plot features (terracing), and site wildfire history. |
| 📄 [`MANFV_Recruitment.csv`](./MANFV_Recruitment.csv) | 📖 [Recruitment Metadata](./MANFV_Recruitment.md) | Regeneration and seedling abundance metrics divided across 4 distinct plant size/height classes. |
| 📄 [`MANFV_Overstory.csv`](./MANFV_Overstory.csv) | 📖 [Overstory Metadata](./MANFV_Overstory.md) | Tree-level metrics including DBH, total height, Crown Base Height (CBH), multi-cardinal bark thickness, and physical damage codes. |
| 📄 [`MANFV_Understory.csv`](./MANFV_Understory.csv) | 📖 [Understory Metadata](./MANFV_Understory.md) | Line-intercept transect intervals capturing fine-scale shrub cover, bare soil distribution, and average patch heights. |
| 📄 [`MANFV_FloorFuels.csv`](./MANFV_FloorFuels.csv) | 📖 [Forest Floor Fuels Metadata](./MANFV_FloorFuels.md) | Downed woody debris metrics categorized via time-lag fuel classes (1-hr, 10-hr, 100-hr) alongside systematic litter and duff depth layers. |
| 📄 [`MANFV_PlantTraits.csv`](./MANFV_PlantTraits.csv) | 📖 [Traits Metadata](./MANFV_PlantTraits.md) | Comprehensive functional plant trait database containing flammability profiles (SAV, Bulk Density, Heat content) and evolutionary traits. |

---

## Methodological Key Notes
* **Feature Classification:** The `Features` metric explicitly tracks land-management; specifically distinguishing between **NT** (Non-Terraced) and **T** (Terraced) slope systems.
* **Data Integration:** All CSV files in this repository are linked via the **`PlotID`** column.
* **Missing Value Log:** Structural voids or values of `0` appearing in canopy closure fields typically reflect total vegetative loss in zones hit with high burn severities (`H`) during the 2013 fire footprint.

